export default {"id":"komplete-level-0","number":0,"title":"What you will use","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"This document is the course map. It is not the lessons.","modules":[{"id":"komplete-m-1-1","code":"1","title":"NI Komplete Kontrol — Course Syllabus","blurb":"This document is the course map. It is not the lessons.","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"komplete-guide-overview","title":"Overview","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"How to read this syllabus overview","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"NI Komplete Kontrol — Course Syllabus","level":1},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Track id (proposed):</strong> <code>komplete-kontrol</code>   <strong>Display title:</strong> NI Komplete Kontrol   <strong>What this course teaches:</strong> How to <strong>use</strong> Native Instruments <strong>Komplete Kontrol</strong> — the software hub, Native Access, the official NI Kontrol keyboards, and officially documented controller setups — to find, load, play, map, record, and sequence instruments, effects, loops, and one-shots in Ableton <strong>Live 12 Standard</strong>.   <strong>Computers:</strong> <strong>Windows</strong> and <strong>macOS</strong> only. This course does not cover any other operating system.   <strong>Primary DAW for studio work:</strong> Ableton <strong>Live 12 Standard</strong> + Operator + Max for Live (this academy’s locked studio).   <strong>Official DAW integrations also documented by Native Instruments for Kontrol S-Series MK3:</strong> Apple Logic Pro; Steinberg Cubase and Nuendo; Ableton Live. Other hosts: follow the official NI Knowledge Base article named in Level 14, and do not invent steps.   <strong>Status:</strong> Syllabus draft for approval. Not lesson content. Not wired into the app.   <strong>Quality bar:</strong> Textbook. Cited. No invented button names, port names, scale counts, or Live features.   <strong>Pedagogy lock:</strong> This course is <strong>what tools can be used and how to operate them</strong> — click-path procedure. It is <strong>not</strong> a course on how NKS, samplers, or scale engines work internally.   <strong>Grounding rule:</strong> Local library (<code>B:\\Documents\\User Manuals\\Other Manuals\\KOMPLETE KONTROL 1.8 Manual.pdf</code> and related NI manuals; <code>B:\\Documents\\TRAINING DOCS</code>) first, then official Native Instruments manuals and Help / Knowledge Base, Ableton Help, and Novation Help only to fill gaps or resolve conflicts. Unsupported or conflicting claims → <code>{type:'gap'}</code>."},{"type":"prose","html":"This document is the course map. It is <strong>not</strong> the lessons."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Map size:</strong> 17 levels (0–16) · 52 modules · Gates A–K · Appendices A–C · Bonus A–C."}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"komplete-m-0-2","code":"0","title":"How to read this syllabus","blurb":"1. Work in order through Levels 0 → 16. Appendices are reference. Bonuses are optional. 2. Every module lists learning outcomes, a lesson table, mustCover / mustNotCover, primary sources, practice, and a checkpoint.","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"komplete-guide-1","title":"How to read this syllabus","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"0. How to read this syllabus","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Work in order through Levels 0 → 16. Appendices are reference. Bonuses are optional.","Every module lists learning outcomes, a lesson table, mustCover / mustNotCover, primary sources, practice, and a checkpoint.","Lessons are named <strong>Lesson X.Y.Z</strong> then a title and a one-sentence description. <strong>X</strong> = level, <strong>Y</strong> = module, <strong>Z</strong> = item. Authoring IDs (<code>kk-l…</code>) are for later lesson files only.","Checkpoints are self-assessment. The desktop academy app cannot watch Komplete Kontrol, Native Access, or Live.","<strong>Hardware is optional for the software path, required only where a module says so.</strong> The software course is complete without an NI keyboard. Hardware modules branch by generation.","Sister courses:","<strong>Mastering Ableton Live 12</strong> — the DAW itself","<strong>Learning the Launchkey MK4 61</strong> — this academy’s Novation keyboard (NKS setup is Bonus A here)","<strong>Piano Playing for Beginners</strong> — how to play the keys","<strong>Drums &amp; Rhythm Programming</strong> — groove as musicianship","<strong>Sound Design Foundations</strong> — synthesis inside the loaded instruments","<strong>Foundations of Music Production</strong> — song architecture","<strong>Building Max for Live Devices</strong> — device building","<strong>AI Tools for Music Production</strong> — other studio tools"],"ordered":true}]},{"type":"step","title":"0.1 Course spine","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;font-family:ui-monospace,monospace\">What Komplete Kontrol is used for → Native Access install →\nfirst standalone sound (Preferences Audio / MIDI) →\nHeader + Browser + Plug-in chain →\nfilter / audition / load a preset →\neight mapped knobs + Plug-in panel →\nadd / reorder / bypass effects →\nPlay Assist: Scale, Key Mode, Chord, Arp →\nloops and one-shots →\nsave and tag user presets →\nload as VST3 in Live 12 Standard →\nrecord notes + automate Scale / Arp →\nif you have an NI keyboard: plug in, firmware, hardware Browser, Light Guide, DAW mode →\nMIDI mode / pedals (generation-specific) →\nother official controllers (Launchkey MK4 = Bonus A) →\ntroubleshooting → capstone</pre>"}]},{"type":"step","title":"0.2 Version honesty (locked)","blocks":[{"type":"table","headers":["Layer","Authority"],"rows":[["Current Komplete Kontrol <strong>software</strong> (Browser, Plug-in chain, Play Assist, Preferences, MIDI Learn, Controller Manager)","Official online <strong>Komplete Kontrol</strong> software manual (Native Instruments tech-manuals hub). The welcome page calls the perform features <strong>Play Assist</strong>. The public product page still says <strong>Smart Play</strong>. <strong>Use the label on the installed build.</strong>"],["Current <strong>Kontrol S-Series MK3</strong> hardware","Official <strong>Kontrol S-Series MK3</strong> / Kontrol MK3 user manual (same hub)."],["Older NI keyboards still in the field","Official A-Series, M32, and S-Series MK2 manuals and download pages. Do not apply MK3 USB-C / four-pedal / PLAY ASSIST-button rules to those units."],["Native Access","Official Native Access page + Komplete Kontrol Setup page. Download buttons on that page (as of syllabus draft): <strong>Windows</strong>, <strong>Mac Intel</strong>, <strong>Apple Silicon</strong>."],["Ableton Live control surfaces","<strong>A-Series / S Mk2 / M32:</strong> Ableton Help <em>Setting up a Native Instruments Komplete Kontrol keyboard</em> (Live 10.0.5+ for A-Series; Live 10.1+ for S Mk2 and M32). <strong>S-Series MK3:</strong> NI MK3 manual — control surface name <strong>Kontrol MK3</strong>, not the older Ableton names."],["Launchkey as an NKS controller","Official Novation Help: <em>How to Setup Komplete Kontrol integration on your NKS Controller</em> (applies to Launchkey MK4)."],["Local PDF <code>KOMPLETE KONTROL 1.8 Manual.pdf</code>","Software version <strong>1.8 (02/2017)</strong>. Historical only. <strong>Do not teach 1.8 click-paths as current.</strong> Use it only to see how much the product has changed."],["Firmware / software build number on a given computer","Native Access + Device Updater / keyboard Settings → General. <strong>Do not freeze a number in this syllabus.</strong>"],["Which Komplete edition the student owns (Select / Standard / Ultimate / individual titles)","The student’s <strong>Native Access</strong> library after login. Titles change. Record what the account shows."]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"Conflicts:"},{"type":"list","items":["<strong>Play Assist vs Smart Play:</strong> software 3.x manual and MK3 hardware manual say Play Assist. Marketing product page still says Smart Play. Teach both names once, then use the installed label.","<strong>Ableton Help vs MK3 manual:</strong> Ableton’s keyboard article names control surfaces <strong>Komplete Kontrol A</strong> and <strong>Komplete Kontrol S Mk 2</strong>. It does <strong>not</strong> name MK3. For MK3, the NI MK3 manual wins: surface <strong>Kontrol MK3</strong>.","<strong>KK Browser page vs Kontakt Browser:</strong> the official KK <em>Browser and presets</em> page also describes Kontakt categories (Instruments, Combined, Tools, Leap). Those are <strong>Kontakt</strong> browser categories. In <strong>Komplete Kontrol</strong> the four product types are <strong>Instruments, Loops, One-shots, Effects</strong>. Teach Kontakt categories only when the keyboard is connected to Kontakt (Level 13 / Appendix).","<strong>Local 1.8 manual vs current software:</strong> current software wins."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"0.3 Suggested pace","blocks":[{"type":"table","headers":["Level","Focus","Duration","Gate"],"rows":[["0","What you will use; software vs keyboard; sister-course borders","1–2 days","—"],["1","Native Access: account, serial, install, first launches","2–4 days","A"],["2","Standalone Preferences and first factory sound","2–4 days","B"],["3","Software layout: Header, views, transport","2–4 days","—"],["4","Browser: filter, audition, load, pin, favorites","3–7 days","C"],["5","Plug-in chain: instrument + effects","3–5 days","D"],["6","Eight knobs, pages, Plug-in panel, MIDI Learn","3–7 days","E"],["7","Play Assist — Scale, Key Mode, Chord","3–7 days","F"],["8","Play Assist — Arpeggiator and MIDI out","3–7 days","G"],["9","Loops, one-shots, Audio plug-in, Sampler","3–5 days","—"],["10","User presets, tags, library folders","2–4 days","H"],["11","Komplete Kontrol as VST3 in Live 12 Standard","3–7 days","I"],["12","Identify your NI keyboard (if any); connect; firmware","2–5 days","—"],["13","Hardware Browser, Plug-in mode, Light Guide","3–7 days","J"],["14","Live mixer / transport from the NI keyboard","3–7 days","—"],["15","MIDI mode, pedals, DIN, third-party / Launchkey","3–7 days","—"],["16","Faults, usage log, capstone","1–2 weeks","K"],["App","MIDI Assignment Editor, Kontakt-from-MK3, Programmer extras","Optional","—"]],"caption":null}]},{"type":"step","title":"0.4 Academy rules this map obeys","blocks":[{"type":"list","items":["Library-grounded. No invented MIDI numbers, knob counts, or Live features.","Full module scaffolding, not a table of contents.","No lesson authoring until this syllabus is approved.","No fake hardware or Live auto-graders.","Project-based. Gate K is a recorded, documented session that used Komplete Kontrol in Live.","Sister-course boundaries respected.","This course does not mention any operating system other than Windows and macOS.","How-to only. One official sentence is enough for “what NKS does for you” (automatic knob mapping). Do not teach the format, protocol, or file internals."],"ordered":false}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"komplete-m-1-3","code":"1","title":"Locked product facts","blurb":"Source: official Komplete Kontrol software welcome page and product page. Komplete Kontrol is not a synthesizer by itself. It loads instruments and effects. Sound design of those instruments belongs to Sound Design Foundations.","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"komplete-guide-2","title":"Locked product facts","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"1.1 What Komplete Kontrol is (official software identity)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Source: official Komplete Kontrol software welcome page and product page."},{"type":"table","headers":["Fact","Statement"],"rows":[["Role","A <strong>free plug-in</strong> (and stand-alone application) that organizes instruments, effects, presets, loops, and samples, and maps them to hardware so you can find, play, and tweak sounds in one place."],["Hosts","Official formats: <strong>VST, VST3, Audio Unit, and AAX</strong>. This academy loads <strong>VST3</strong> in Live 12 Standard. <strong>Audio Unit</strong> is a <strong>macOS</strong> format only."],["Controllers","Official: works with <strong>any MIDI controller</strong>, or with <strong>mouse and computer keyboard</strong>. Tightest integration is with official <strong>KOMPLETE KONTROL / Kontrol</strong> keyboards."],["Library","Browser shows presets from <strong>Komplete</strong> instruments and effects <strong>and</strong> any <strong>NKS-compatible</strong> plug-in installed on the computer."],["NKS, one sentence (official)","NKS (Native Kontrol Standard) enables <strong>automatic mapping of the knobs</strong> on a supported controller to plug-in parameters as soon as you load a preset in Komplete Kontrol. You do not have to assign those knobs with MIDI Learn first."],["Play features","Official wording: map the keyboard to <strong>over 100</strong> scales and modes; play chords with one finger; create arpeggios. Software 3.x name: <strong>Play Assist</strong>. Product-page name: <strong>Smart Play</strong>."]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"Komplete Kontrol is <strong>not</strong> a synthesizer by itself. It <strong>loads</strong> instruments and effects. Sound design of those instruments belongs to <strong>Sound Design Foundations</strong>."}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.2 The two official layers","blocks":[{"type":"table","headers":["Layer","What the student uses it for","Required?"],"rows":[["<strong>Komplete Kontrol software</strong>","Browse, load, chain, Play Assist, save presets, run as plug-in in Live","<strong>Yes</strong>"],["<strong>Native Access</strong>","Download, activate, update NI software; add keyboard serial","<strong>Yes</strong>"],["<strong>NI Kontrol keyboard</strong> (A-Series, M32, S-Series MK2, or S-Series MK3)","Hardware browse, Light Guide (S-Series), DAW control, Play Assist from the keys","<strong>No</strong> for software Gates A–I. <strong>Yes</strong> for hardware Gates J and the hardware clauses of Gate K"],["<strong>Other MIDI controller</strong>","Controller Manager templates, or MIDI Learn","Optional"],["<strong>Launchkey MK4</strong>","Official Novation NKS Custom Modes + Controller Manager","Optional (Bonus A; sister course owns the Launchkey itself)"],["<strong>Kontakt</strong>","MK3 can browse Kontakt as well as Komplete Kontrol. Kontakt itself is not this course.","Optional overlap — see Appendix C"]],"caption":null}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.3 Official NI keyboard families (identify, do not mix rules)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Teach this table so the student does <strong>not</strong> apply MK3 rules to an A-Series unit."},{"type":"table","headers":["Family","Official sizes / keybed (product + MK3 manual)","Display / Light Guide","Live control-surface name (documented)"],"rows":[["<strong>Kontrol S-Series MK3</strong> (current flagship)","<strong>S49</strong> and <strong>S61</strong>: semi-weighted Fatar, <strong>polyphonic aftertouch</strong>. <strong>S88</strong>: fully-weighted hammer-action Fatar, <strong>polyphonic aftertouch</strong>. Same controls beyond the keybed.","High-res color display + <strong>Light Guide</strong>","<strong>Kontrol MK3</strong>. Ports: <code>KONTROL S[xx] MK3 (DAW)</code> on <strong>macOS</strong>; <code>KONTROL S[xx] MK3 (Port 2)</code> on <strong>Windows</strong>."],["<strong>Komplete Kontrol S-Series MK2</strong>","49 / 61 / 88 (use the student’s unit + official MK2 manual)","Two high-res color screens + <strong>Light Guide</strong> (product page / MK2 docs)","Ableton: <strong>Komplete Kontrol S Mk 2</strong>"],["<strong>Komplete Kontrol A-Series</strong>","<strong>A25 / A49 / A61</strong>, semi-weighted (product page)","OLED (product page). No Light Guide on the product-page description.","Ableton: <strong>Komplete Kontrol A</strong> (Live 10.0.5+)"],["<strong>Komplete Kontrol M32</strong>","<strong>32</strong> compact keys, USB bus-powered (official M32 page)","OLED (product page). No Light Guide on the official M32 page.","Ableton: included with S Mk2 from Live 10.1 (Ableton Help lists M32 with S Mk2)"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"<code>{type:'gap'}</code> — this academy has <strong>not</strong> locked a single keyboard SKU. The student writes their model and serial (from the unit / Native Access / MK3 Settings → General) in Lesson 12.1.1. If they have <strong>no</strong> NI keyboard, they skip hardware-only lessons and still complete the software + Live path."},{"type":"prose","html":"S-Series <strong>MK1</strong> is the generation documented by the local <strong>1.8</strong> manual. Do not teach MK1 as current. If a student still has MK1, <code>{type:'gap'}</code>: confirm Live 12 control-surface support from Ableton/NI at lesson time; do not invent it."}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.4 Official MK3 hardware facts (only if the student has MK3)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Source: MK3 <em>Keyboard Overview</em> and <em>Setting Up Your Keyboard</em>."},{"type":"table","headers":["Item","Official fact"],"rows":[["Top-panel controls","SHIFT; UNDO (Redo); QUANTIZE; Page left/right; <strong>PLAY ASSIST</strong>; SETTINGS (MIDI); eight knobs + eight buttons + display; <strong>BROWSER</strong>; <strong>PLUG IN</strong>; <strong>DAW</strong>; <strong>4-D encoder</strong>; PREVIOUS / NEXT; transport"],["Keybed extras","Light Guide; Pitch wheel; Modulation wheel; Touch Strip (default MIDI <strong>CC #11</strong> Expression); <strong>FIXED VEL</strong> (fixed velocity <strong>127</strong>); OCTAVE down/up; SHIFT + OCTAVE = semitone"],["Rear","ON switch; USB-C <strong>HOST</strong>; USB-C <strong>Power</strong> (only if the computer/hub cannot supply enough power); four 1/4\" pedals: <strong>SUSTAIN, EXPRESSION, ASSIGN 1, ASSIGN 2</strong>; 5-pin <strong>MIDI IN</strong> and <strong>MIDI OUT</strong>"],["USB to a USB-C computer","Included USB-C cable, barrel-style end into HOST, other end into the computer, then ON"],["USB to a USB-A-only computer","Official extra (not in the box): USB-C female to USB-A male adapter/cable <strong>plus</strong> a USB-C power supply <strong>5 V, 7.5 W or higher, 1.5 A or higher</strong> into the Power socket"],["Pedals","All four sockets accept <strong>continuous or switch</strong> pedals. Configure in Settings. Official advice: keep SUSTAIN as Switch and EXPRESSION as Continuous unless the student has a reason to change them"],["MIDI DIN port names in software","Input: <code>KONTROL S[xx] MK3 (MIDI)</code> (<strong>macOS</strong>) or <code>MIDIIN3 (KONTROL S[xx] MK3)</code> (<strong>Windows</strong>). Output: <code>KONTROL S[xx] MK3 (MIDI)</code> (<strong>macOS</strong>) or <code>MIDIOUT3 (KONTROL S[xx] MK3)</code> (<strong>Windows</strong>)"]],"caption":null}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.5 Official software layout (current)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Source: <em>Komplete Kontrol Overview</em>, <em>Using Plug-ins</em>, <em>Browser and presets</em>."},{"type":"table","headers":["Area","What the student uses it for"],"rows":[["<strong>Header</strong>","Main menu, Preset display, transport and volume, show/hide Browser / Perform / Plug-in chain"],["<strong>Plug-in chain</strong>","Slot <strong>1</strong> = instrument <strong>or</strong> sample. Slot <strong>2 onward</strong> = effects only. Signal flow <strong>left → right</strong>."],["<strong>Browser</strong>","Instruments, Loops, One-shots, Effects. Tags, product tiles, search, audition, favorites, factory/user"],["<strong>Perform panel</strong>","SCALE on/off + parameters; ARP on/off + parameters"],["<strong>Plug-in panel</strong>","Eight mapped knobs per page; Edit mode to remap"],["<strong>Instrument views</strong>","<strong>Default View</strong> (on load). <strong>Additional View</strong> via Header <strong>+</strong> / View button. <strong>Edit View</strong> for <strong>REAKTOR</strong> and <strong>Kontakt</strong> instruments (full app). Switch also from Main menu → View."]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"Stand-alone transport in the Header: <strong>Play</strong>, <strong>Reset</strong>, <strong>Tempo</strong>. When Komplete Kontrol is a <strong>plug-in</strong>, those controls are <strong>grayed out</strong> and the host tempo/transport win."}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.6 Official Browser click-facts (software)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Source: <em>Browser and presets</em>."},{"type":"table","headers":["Control","How to use it"],"rows":[["Open Browser","Click the Browser icon in the Header"],["Product Type","First slot: Instruments, Loops, or One-shots. Other slots: Effects only"],["Search field","Filters by preset name, author, Brand / Character / Sound Type tags, product, bank"],["Tag filters","Brand, Sound Type (Type + Subtype), Character. Multi-select: <strong>Shift+click</strong>, or <strong>Ctrl+click</strong> (<strong>Windows</strong>) / <strong>command+click</strong> (<strong>macOS</strong>)"],["Product tiles","Click a tile to filter. Hover → <strong>&gt;</strong> loads the <strong>first</strong> preset of that product"],["Results","<strong>Click</strong> = audition (does not load). <strong>Double-click</strong> = load into the current slot. Up/Down arrows move the selection"],["Audition","On by default. Speaker icon mutes it. Volume control sits with the audition controls"],["Pin","Off by default (Browser closes on load). Pin keeps it open"],["Favorites","Star filters the list to favorites"],["User Content","On = user presets only. Off = factory only"],["Reset","Clears brand, product, bank, Sound Type, Character, User, Favorites"],["Info (I)","Properties and tags of the selected preset; tag user presets here"],["Save user preset","Select the slot → Main menu <strong>File → Save</strong> or <strong>Save As…</strong>"]],"caption":null}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.7 Official Play Assist facts (software)","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Source: <em>Using Scales and the Arpeggiator</em>."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Open:</strong> Header → Perform panel button."},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Scale on:</strong> checkbox left of <strong>SCALE</strong>. Click the <strong>SCALE</strong> label to edit."},{"type":"table","headers":["Parameter group","Official values the course must teach how to set"],"rows":[["Root Note","C, C#, D, D#, E, F, F#, G, G#, A, A#, B"],["Bank / Type","Each Bank has <strong>15</strong> Types. Banks documented: <strong>Main, Modes, Jazz, World, 5-Tone, Modern, Major, Minor</strong>. Default example: Root <strong>C</strong>, Bank <strong>Main</strong>, Type <strong>Major</strong>"],["KEY MODE","<strong>Guide</strong>, <strong>Mapped</strong> (default), <strong>Easy</strong>"],["Easy mode","White keys only play the scale. Black keys are inactive. Root is mapped to <strong>middle C (C3)</strong>. Chromatic in Easy = same mapping as Mapped"],["CHORD Mode","<strong>Off</strong>, <strong>Harmonizer (Harm)</strong>, <strong>Chord Set (Chd Set)</strong>"],["Harmonizer Type","Octave; 1-3; 1-5; 1-3-5; 1-4-5; 1-3-5-7; 1-4-7"],["Chord Set Type","Maj 1–8, Min 1–8. Scale Type and Key Mode are <strong>unavailable</strong> in Chord Set"],["Chord Position","Root; −1 to −8; +1 to +8; <strong>Auto</strong>"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Arp on:</strong> checkbox left of <strong>ARP</strong>."},{"type":"table","headers":["Parameter group","Official values / job"],"rows":[["MAIN Mode","<strong>Arp</strong> or <strong>Note Repeat</strong>"],["MAIN Type (Arp only)","<strong>Up, Down, Up &amp; Down, Order Played, Chord</strong>"],["RHYTHM","Rate, Sequence, Swing"],["OTHER","Octaves, Dynamic, Gate"],["ADVANCED","Retrigger, Repeat, Offset, Inversion"],["RANGE","Min. Key, Max. Key"],["HOLD","Latches the sequence. Switching Arp off and on again keeps HOLD if it was on"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"Incoming MIDI from the DAW is also mapped through Scale. Example from the manual: Root C, pattern C–D–D♯ stays C–D–D♯ in Chromatic and becomes C–D–E in Major."}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.8 Official MIDI / automation facts","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Source: <em>Automation and MIDI Control</em>; <em>Preferences</em>."},{"type":"table","headers":["Fact","Statement"],"rows":[["MIDI Clock in","<strong>Komplete Kontrol does not receive MIDI Clock.</strong> As a plug-in it follows the DAW tempo."],["Scale / Arp MIDI out","Notes generated by Scale and Arp are sent from the stand-alone app <strong>and</strong> from the plug-in, so they can be recorded in Live or routed to another MIDI instrument."],["Formats that send that MIDI out","Stand-alone, <strong>VST</strong>, <strong>VST3</strong>, <strong>AAX</strong>. The <strong>AU</strong> plug-in does <strong>not</strong> support MIDI output. In this academy use <strong>VST3</strong> on both Windows and macOS."],["Automation IDs (Perform)","Official reserved IDs include 000 (instance recognition / focus follow), 001 Scale On/Off, 002 Root Note, 003 Scale Type, 004 Key Mode, 006 Chord Mode, 007 Chord Type, 026 Arp On/Off, 027–041 Arp Mode through Hold. Teach students to record these from Live’s automation, not to memorize every number."],["MIDI Learn (third-party)","Header <strong>MIDI</strong> → Knobs page / Buttons page. Preferences → MIDI → enable the controller. Takeover <strong>Pickup</strong> prevents jumps. Buttons on the hardware must be in <strong>Trigger</strong> mode, not Toggle, for MIDI mapping."],["Share mapping","Map once; new instances inherit it. Instances already open need the DAW closed and reopened."],["Controller Manager","Main menu → <strong>Controller → Controller Manager</strong>. Double-click the controller (or hover → arrow) to load its template. Header icon shows the brand."],["Controller Manager lock","<strong>Not accessible when an NI Kontrol keyboard is connected.</strong>"],["MIDI Assignment Editor","Officially available for <strong>S-Series MK2, A-Series, M32</strong>. <strong>Not</strong> listed for MK3. MK3 MIDI assignments live in <strong>Settings</strong> (wheels, strip, pedals)."]],"caption":null}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.9 Official Live 12 setup facts","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>All NI keyboards (Ableton Help, A / S Mk2 / M32):</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Install the <strong>latest</strong> Komplete Kontrol from Native Access. Ableton: you must install it <strong>even if you do not use the plug-in</strong>, or the control surface will not work.","Connect the keyboard.","Launch Live — it should auto-activate.","If not: Preferences → <strong>Link/MIDI</strong> (Ableton article says <strong>Link MIDI</strong>; MK3 manual says <strong>Link/MIDI</strong>). Choose <strong>Komplete Kontrol A</strong> or <strong>Komplete Kontrol S Mk 2</strong>, then the keyboard’s input and output ports."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>S-Series MK3 (NI MK3 manual — this is the MK3 path):</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Connect and switch the keyboard on.","Launch Live.","Preferences → Link/MIDI.","Unused slot: Control Surface = <strong>Kontrol MK3</strong>.","Input and Output = <code>KONTROL S[xx] MK3 (DAW)</code> (<strong>macOS</strong>) or <code>KONTROL S[xx] MK3 (Port 2)</code> (<strong>Windows</strong>)."],"ordered":true},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Plug-in path (every student):</strong>"},{"type":"list","items":["Live 12 Standard Browser → Plug-ins → <strong>VST3</strong> → Komplete Kontrol.","MIDI from the keyboard (or computer keys) onto that track. Record-arm the track.","Do not also fight the control-surface ports: the DAW port is for mixer/transport; the notes port is for playing. Follow the official port names for the student’s generation."],"ordered":false}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.10 Official Native Access / first-install facts","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Source: <em>Komplete Kontrol Setup</em>; Native Access product page."},{"type":"table","headers":["Step","Official action"],"rows":[["1","Download Native Access for <strong>Windows</strong>, <strong>Mac Intel</strong>, or <strong>Apple Silicon</strong>. Log in (or create) an NI account. Check Installation Preferences."],["2","<strong>Add serial</strong> — keyboard serial from the flyer in the box or the underside of the keyboard. Wait; use Refresh if install is not ready."],["3","Install <strong>Komplete Kontrol</strong> software, the Komplete instruments/effects the account owns, and <strong>MASCHINE Essentials</strong>."],["3b","<strong>Launch Komplete Kontrol and MASCHINE Essentials once in stand-alone</strong> before using them as plug-ins, so preset databases are created."],["4","Connect the keyboard and run the <strong>Device Updater</strong> for firmware."],["Online","Native Access currently requires being <strong>online</strong> and logged in."],["Legacy","Native Access page: <strong>legacy software not supported</strong>."]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"Serial-less software-only students (no NI keyboard): install Komplete Kontrol from the account / free download path on the official KK product page. <code>{type:'gap'}</code> if that free-download wizard changes — re-read the page at lesson time."}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.11 Official plug-in-chain click-facts","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"Source: <em>Using Plug-ins</em>."},{"type":"table","headers":["Job","Clicks"],"rows":[["Open chain","Plug-in chain button in the Header"],["Load instrument in slot 1","<strong>+</strong> → pick an instrument from the list. Only instruments (or a sample) in slot 1"],["Load effect","After slot 1 is filled, click the empty slot (Browser switches to Effects) and load; or <strong>+</strong> at the end"],["Replace","Arrow at the bottom of the slot → pick another plug-in (loads default state)"],["Main menu load","Instruments submenu <strong>replaces</strong> the instrument. Effects submenu <strong>appends</strong> a new slot"],["Missing plug-ins","Preferences → Plug-ins → <strong>Locations</strong> — add folders, <strong>Rescan</strong>. Manager checkboxes enable/disable"],["Bypass effect","Hover slot → Bypass (top left). Image greys out"],["Remove effect","Hover slot → Remove (top right)"],["Reorder effects","Drag slot; white line is the drop point. Slot 1 stays the instrument/sample"],["Scroll","Big arrows appear when the chain is wider than the window"],["Loops","Loading content type <strong>Loop</strong> opens the <strong>Audio</strong> plug-in in slot 1"],["Audio engines documented","<strong>Re-pitch</strong> (tempo via playback rate; pitch follows; cheaper CPU; good for unpitched drums). <strong>Stretch</strong> (tempo and pitch independent; more CPU). <strong>Formant</strong> is the third official engine name — teach the control from the installed GUI; do not invent Formant behaviour beyond the official page."],["Audio Tune","−36 to +36 semitones (Stretch and Formant only)"],["Audio Pitchbend","−12 to +12 relative to Tune (Stretch and Formant only)"],["Start/End markers","Software only"]],"caption":null}]},{"type":"step","title":"1.12 Default musical / hardware values that are documented","blocks":[{"type":"table","headers":["Item","Default","Source"],"rows":[["KEY MODE","<strong>Mapped</strong>","Scale chapter"],["Scale example","Root <strong>C</strong>, Bank <strong>Main</strong>, Type <strong>Major</strong>","Scale chapter"],["CHORD Mode","<strong>Off</strong> until the student turns it on","Scale chapter"],["FIXED VEL (MK3)","Off; when on, velocity <strong>127</strong>","MK3 overview"],["Aftertouch (MK3)","<strong>Polyphonic</strong> (also Monophonic, Off)","MK3 Settings"],["Velocity curve (MK3)","<strong>Linear</strong>; Soft 3–1 / Hard 1–3","MK3 Settings"],["Touch Strip default","MIDI <strong>CC #11</strong> (Expression)","MK3 overview"],["Audition","On","Browser"],["Browser Pin","Off","Browser"],["Usage data tracking","On until the student unchecks it (Preferences → General; MK3 Settings → Usage Data)","Preferences; MK3 Settings"],["MIDI 1.0 vs 2.0 (MK3)","Selectable in Settings → Hardware page 2. Confirm host/OS support at lesson time from Windows or macOS docs + NI Knowledge Base. Do not invent Live 12 MIDI 2.0 behaviour.","MK3 Settings"]],"caption":null}]}],"minutes":17}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"komplete-m-0-1-2","code":"0.1","title":"— Product map","blurb":"— Product map","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"komplete-kk-l0-1-1","title":"Product map","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Module 0.1 — Product map","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Outcomes:</strong> The student can name the software, Native Access, and (if present) their keyboard, and can say in one sentence what each is <strong>used for</strong>."},{"type":"table","headers":["Lesson","Title","Description","Authoring ID"],"rows":[["0.1.1","The job","Use Komplete Kontrol to find a sound, load it, play it, twist the eight mapped knobs, and land that performance in Live.","<code>kk-l0-1-1</code>"],["0.1.2","Software vs keyboard","The software is required. The NI keyboard is the official hardware partner. Mouse + computer keys are enough to start.","<code>kk-l0-1-2</code>"],["0.1.3","It does not make sound by itself","Load an instrument (or loop/one-shot). No instrument = no audio. Same idea as a MIDI keyboard with an empty Live track.","<code>kk-l0-1-3</code>"],["0.1.4","NKS in one sentence","Official: knobs map automatically when you load an NKS preset. Stop there.","<code>kk-l0-1-4</code>"],["0.1.5","Play Assist / Smart Play","Two official names for Scale + Chord + Arp. Use the installed label.","<code>kk-l0-1-5</code>"],["0.1.6","What this course will not do","No synthesis theory. No piano method. No “how the browser database is built.”","<code>kk-l0-1-6</code>"],["0.1.7","Local 1.8 PDF","Show the 2017 date. File it as history. Current clicks come from the 3.x online manual.","<code>kk-l0-1-7</code>"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>mustCover:</strong> job → tool table; 1.8 is not current.   <strong>mustNotCover:</strong> NKS file format; neural/tagging theory; other OS.   <strong>Sources:</strong> KK welcome; product page; local 1.8 title page.   <strong>Practice:</strong> Student writes a three-line “I will use X to do Y” card.   <strong>Checkpoint:</strong> Can point at software vs keyboard vs Native Access."}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"komplete-m-0-2-3","code":"0.2","title":"— Sister course borders and studio lock","blurb":"— Sister course borders and studio lock","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"komplete-kk-l0-2-1","title":"Sister-course borders and studio lock","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Module 0.2 — Sister-course borders and studio lock","blocks":[{"type":"table","headers":["Lesson","Title","Description","Authoring ID"],"rows":[["0.2.1","Live 12 Standard","This course inserts KK as VST3 and uses Live’s Link/MIDI page. Live itself is the Live course.","<code>kk-l0-2-1</code>"],["0.2.2","Launchkey MK4","Playing, Components, Scale/Chord/Arp <strong>on the Launchkey</strong> stay in the Launchkey course. NKS Custom Modes into KK are Bonus A here.","<code>kk-l0-2-2</code>"],["0.2.3","Piano / drums / sound design","Keys, groove, and synth architecture are those courses. KK is how you <strong>call up</strong> the sounds.","<code>kk-l0-2-3</code>"],["0.2.4","Kontakt vs KK","MK3 can drive Kontakt <strong>or</strong> KK. This course operates KK. Kontakt Multi/Tools/Leap stay optional/appendix.","<code>kk-l0-2-4</code>"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>mustCover:</strong> VST3 + Live 12 Standard; Launchkey is a sister course.   <strong>mustNotCover:</strong> teaching Kontakt 8 as this course.   <strong>Sources:</strong> this syllabus §1; sister Desktop syllabi.   <strong>Practice:</strong> Student lists the one DAW and one KK job for this course.   <strong>Checkpoint:</strong> No “we’ll also learn Massive X from scratch here.”"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
